oing to give us some really  valuable  insight in terms of um you know where  people are in terms of vaccinations  testing support for self-isolation and  just about  you know the impact of covered really  and how people are feeling so  the first day was yesterday went really  well and the team spoke to around 100  parents so um by the end of the week we  should have some really really good  insight  from that activity um i just wanted to  just mention voice of bme again  as we mentioned previously they they  continue to make a real difference  through the work they're doing with the  practices in the north  uh and they're talking to people who  were initially hesitant about taking the  vaccine  giving them facts and reassurance asking  i think it'd be better to support it  and then booking them a vaccination if  they want to go ahead with one and  today i think the latest information i  have is that 79 people  change their minds have now decided to  be vaccinated so just a real good  achievement there from voice of bme and  we are currently having conversations  with them around  um working in the partington area to  help increase uh vaccine uptake there as  well so we've got our meeting with them  next week to look at that  and uh in terms of further activities as  has already been mentioned we've had  some real  success in terms of increase in the  vaccination uptake with the asian  communities  and so our focus is uh obviously to  continue with that work  also to focus on communities where  there's still lower uptake so  we are looking at first some things  we've been doing is in terms of uh  cross-boundary promotion of clinics  uh where they're aimed at specific  communities so some of these are held  over the border in hume or wally range  but we're promoting those clinics  we are working with the um khan which is  the caribbean and african health network  and we're looking to help do some  further work with them because they've  got a real presence and reach 